> 
> >   DUMP: Protocol to remote tape server botched (code "bash: rmt: command
> > not found").
> > rdump: Lost connection to remote host.
> >   DUMP: Bad return code from dump: 1
> 
> Remote dumps work by 'rsh'ing over to the machine and then running a program
> called 'rmt' (which stands for remote tape!) on the machine with the tape drive.
> Most machines tend to have it in /etc/rmt; check that the machine with the
> tape drive has rmt

Actually, I believe it is more like this:

rdump calls 'rmt' on the local machine, which 'rsh'es to the remote
machine and runs 'mt' (Which stands for Magnetic Tape).  So check to make
sure you have rmt installed on the *local* machine.  (rmt standing for
Remote Magnetic Tape :) )

--Randy


