Hello!
I just stepped into some trouble getting my new SX164@533MHz to work. It
still does not work perfectly well but one problem is solved. Here is my
little errata. If a fix for those problems is known I would be very glad to
be notified ;) Especially the interrupt hangs and the memory corruptions are
really bad. I wonder why noone else noticed this by now. The SX164 is not
that new anymore...
Here we go:

Floppy DMA still does not work up to kernel 2.1.119
Fix for 2.1.119:
after line 107 of linux/arch/alpha/kernel/sys_sx164.c the follwing two lines
must be added (this is from Eric Lee Green and adapted to 2.1.119):

static void
sx164_init_irq(void)
{
        outb(0, DMA1_RESET_REG);
        outb(0, DMA2_RESET_REG);
+       outb(DMA_MODE_CASCADE, DMA2_MODE_REG);
+       outb(0, DMA2_MASK_REG);

        if (alpha_using_srm) {


After starting XQuake and beginning a new game system freezes completely
until the mouse is moved, i.e. no ping is answered and all other hw-interrupts
seem not to reach the kernel! Those 'hangs' also occur later in game and
sometimes cause the machine to block completely.

Some SVGAlib applications crash the machine at once, causing the system to
reboot immediately at startup of SVGAlib application.

Some application cause memory corruptions, like the MPEG-1 video player
'mtvp' from http://www.mpegtv.com/. This runs fine on other Alpha systems!
Memory corruptions are also reported from other applications that use
mmapped files and pthreads (see comp.os.linux.alpha). The corruptions cause
the application itself to fail and sometimes causes other unrelated
applications to fail too! Compiling a kernel while playing video for example
ends with a sig 11 or seg-fault.


Hopefully someone more fimiliar with the SX164 hardware can sort those
problems out and offer a fix...
CU
