> On Sat, 5 Sep 1998, Richard Henderson wrote:
> 
> > > Thought Alphas cannot generate denormalized outputs, at least with HW.
> >
> > This is true.
> 
> Is it valid code to use another architecture to generate some floating
> point data, save it in a binary file and then load it back on an Alpha?
> If so, would it be valid for that file to contain denormalised data
> values?
> 

Sounds plausible but if I have algorithms that
might do that, I always look for a switch to set
underflows to zero, which would avoid the problem.

Ask yourself under what sort of conditions would a
de-normalized number be more useful to an algorithm
than just forcing it to zero??

Also, how would the answer change if you increased your 
FP precision vs using de-normalized numbers or zeros?


Wes


