And in mine:

>  18 .got          00010230  000000000043ec98  000000000043ec98  0033ec98  2**3

My .got exceeds the maximum allowed size, because my usual compilation
technique for my big C++ library is to cat all the files together and
let it rip -- the savings on debugging symbols and compilation time is
immense. But the resulting .o has too many symbols for the modern
binutils (".got exceeds 64K blah blah...").

So now I'm trying to figure out if separate compilation breaks because
my code is broken, or egcs is broken.

The total size of my project is 300k lines. egcs couldn't compile it
due to egcs bugs until 1.0.2, but I have hopes that they're testing
well enough that future versions will stay unbroken.

Life is just different with big C++ programs.

-- g


