On Thu, 10 Sep 1998, Paul Tomblin wrote:

> Can anybody explain why cua0 would work when ttyS0 doesn't?  I thought they

Sure can't.  You shouldn't be using cua* at all.  Maybe you ought to read
linux/Documentation/devices.txt and make sure you have your {maj,min}
numbers all in order and such.

> were basically the exact same kernel driver, but the "cua0" had some extra
> locking logic for the benefit of uucp?

I don't think so.  UUCP-style locking deals with something else IIRC.  The
difference that I've heard is that one is for dial-in and the other for
dial-out, but because of UUCP-style locking, a dial-out would appear free
when it was really being used by a dial-in.  Something like that.

Christopher


