Wes Bauske wrote:
> 
> Doesn't that get_unaligned() routine work for places other than the
> kernel??

From a recent posting by Richard Henderson get_unaligned() is
an "abominable casting hack" (or something close) and it should not
work at all with current compilers.  That it still happens to work
is a small miracle and/or a compiler bug.

In the case I was interested (kernel and fdisk throwing "unaligned"
tantrums when checking partition data) a cure consisted from
adding 'packed' attribute to 'partition' structure.

  Michal


