With regards to your message at 08:01 PM 09-13-98 METDST, furio ercolessi.
Where you stated:
>> could you just set:
>> OsLoadOptions= boot sda5:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/sda5 mem=224M
>> ?
>> according to the bootprompt howto 'mem=' is a valid argument to the
>> kernel.
>> or do you really need to set it with MILO for some other reason?
>
>For reasons that escape my comprehension, the Samsung UX
>(aka Ruffian) ignores "mem=" as a boot parameter.  It requires
>memory to be set up in advance by MILO.  
>Anyway thanks for the tip.
>
>furio
Correct. ARCSBIOS is NOT ARC or AlphaBIOS. It is a device set up by
Deskstation when they devised Ruffian, and as they basically went broke in
mid-project, many areas are partially unfinished, or not even implemented
at all.
Parameters passed are severely limited.


