> kernel on a floppy if I can managed to create one).

There are a few things different with the i386 platform for compiling
kernels.
First there are a few patches that you want to apply or need to apply for
2.0.* kernels. They can be found somewhere on gatekeeper.dec.com, in
ftp://gatekeeper.dec.com/pub/Digital/Linux-Alpha/Kernels/ if I am correct.
Beside that, make xconfig and make menuconfig are broken on the Alpha
platform, for ages (somebody please fix this !!), use make config. 

