> [...]
> So we still have weird problems on high memory systems;
> and this one does not depend on Ruffian...

The point is, how much is "high"?  I have problems with 256MB,
and somebody else reported similar problems with 128MB.

I tend to think that there is an error in the port of
the virtual memory code for these machines, which in some cases
for fortuitous circumstances does not prevent machines from
operating regularly.

