> you don't get the device to shut up, you'll continually get sent back
> to the interrupt handler.

I've sure seen my share of interrupt locks on my i960rp based system.
First thing I would do is probe (logic probe will do) the IRQA# lines
of all the PCI cards, 'cause they are easy. It gets harder after that,
because probing for any interrupt source on the base board requires a
bit more knowledge of the motherboard then I have. Schematics would be
really nice:-)

(Yes, I *do* debug my software with a 'scope and logic analyzer. Doesn't
everybody?-)

If I have time this weekend I will see what I can figure out. I have the
hardware tools to check PCI slots, and *might* be able to track down
some other potential interrupt sources as well.
